  "changes": [
    "RemoteDataBackend.resolveEvidence uses the producer POST current-storage resolver, with a distinct resolution.receipt.json and all 21 shared wire cases.",
    "Immutable locator, metadata, unknown option and encoded JSON validation before headers/I/O, including revalidation after caller-owned toJSON serialization.",
    "Configured authentication/archive headers retained; caller tenant/archive/visibility fields rejected. Resolution predicates and archived inclusion do not widen the remote GET search subset.",
    "Request no-store and redirect denial; response JSON/no-store/strict schema/well-formed UTF-8/exact span-length validation with a bounded growing buffer.",
    "One 30-second deadline and optional AbortSignal cover header lookup, fetch and streaming. Bounded HTTP status or transport/aborted errors retain no raw response text, URL, cause or input.",
    "Producer owns current authorization/unit/source/full-text digest checks; a partial response cannot independently prove the parent text digest. No detail rebinding.",
    "Clean installed public package validates nine resolution checks plus existing evidence/REST/capability/shard gates. Historical evidence and GET REST receipts unchanged.",
    "Current implementation receipt refreshed after build and complete portable conformance; published fixtures and releases not replaced."
  ],
